{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/prompt.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:06:48.231266Z","id":"b041ea0214dec031a8df84775b2ec9e7cea7beb5e8eef5ad12882ffaba34a5b2","body":{"detail":"PromptBuilder.change writes CommentContext.anchorLine verbatim after \"Anchored on: \", while the comment body and author are JSON-quoted. The anchor's quote is page text (which the agent itself wrote, or which a document rendered), so it can carry instruction-like text or newlines that break the prompt's layout. Whoever renders anchorLine (the feedback worker in lib/agent/loop.dart) should JSON-quote the quote part and cut it to 120 characters, or PromptBuilder should quote the whole line.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"72d1d0918b41b8390e360792f83ec31640d348c6f9cf350c9e988e603fd4dee8"},"summary":"The anchor line goes into the change prompt unquoted, though its quote is text taken from the page","tags":["security","prompt","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_result.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:06:48.231479Z","id":"1d76d70ec363a2b25c56d46a32ab274f275e2b1a62ef7c55878a3680785520bb","body":{"detail":"Two FileWrite entries with the same path, or a path in both files and removed, pass validation (the rules in docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app.md Task F4a do not list them). The code that applies a result (applyResult) must give these a defined meaning (last write wins; removed after files, or a refusal) and test it, or validateResult should refuse them with a named reason so the one retry can fix them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":221},"end":{"line":240},"content_hash":"3199a4dbb21944535df116037febfe986383332e2f390bd23376fd97c4286edc"},"summary":"validateResult does not refuse a path written twice in files, or both written and removed","tags":["validation","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_result.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:28.968137Z","id":"02408d6b80a7ca649671c41c4a511cca863557e94ffc752a5601f0aa5941d775","body":{"detail":"Failure: a result with db [{op: 'set', collection: 'runs', doc_id: 'my run', data_json: '{}'}] (or doc_id '..', 'é', a 201-byte segment, or a collection deeper than 16 segments) passes validateResult. The daemon's segment rule (crates/clax-core/src/db.rs:88-96, segment_ok: ASCII letters, digits and _ - . ~ : @ +, 1 to 200 bytes, not . or ..; db.rs:98-117: at most 1000 bytes and 16 segments per path) refuses it with invalid_argument. Spec section 3.6 applies a change as publish, then the db operations, so the new version is already live when docs:batch fails: a shape migration the new page depends on never runs, and a daemon 400 is not a validation failure, so the one retry with the failure named does not happen. validateResult should apply the same segment and length rules to collection + '/' + doc_id, naming the bad segment, with a test case per rule in test/agent/edit_result_test.dart.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":262},"end":{"line":289},"content_hash":"129583594e693adaa0ba0265c5fc87b263e7865675e1d38445b7ad5c9050ed0a"},"summary":"validateResult accepts db collection and doc_id segments that the daemon refuses, so a change publishes and then its db writes fail","tags":["review","validation","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_result.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:28.968319Z","id":"5f0eadcd4a81e91d233c2802156851d44716a1dd32c303f11ab8589d44296b9a","body":{"detail":"_checkPath refuses code units below 0x20 and 0x7f only. crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs:96-117 (check_path) also refuses every char::is_control character (U+0080 to U+009F) and U+2028/U+2029. Such a path passes validation and the publish or create then fails with invalid_path, which is not retried with the reason named. Mirror the daemon's rule (and add test cases for '\\u0085' and '\\u2028').","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":302},"end":{"line":308},"content_hash":"629ba97c204ed9557d56e9218c01cc470ae9101a14151ad960ff01f5aef74111"},"summary":"File paths with C1 control characters or U+2028/U+2029 pass validateResult but the daemon refuses them","tags":["review","validation","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_schema.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:28.968419Z","id":"0f5e9d556f451b80d34ae63ddb6a29c1833e998e32330255becffb5eff044536","body":{"detail":"claude 2.1.296 implements --json-schema as a synthetic StructuredOutput tool that the model must call (strings in the binary: 'StructuredOutput enforcement failed', 'structuredOutputTool'), passed separately from the tools option, so it probably survives --tools \"\", but nothing in `claude --help` says so and no test exercises it. The schema itself is plain JSON Schema with a top-level object, which that path accepts. The ClaudeCliBackend's integration run must confirm that a `--tools \"\" --json-schema <editSchema>` call returns `structured_output`, and fall back to parsing `result` if it does not (spec section 3.6).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":9},"content_hash":"7c4f21fb9cdc049af71174832ed6c1e28607669a87b512e96c980dc7ab0402fa"},"summary":"The schema's use as claude -p --json-schema together with --tools \"\" is unverified","tags":["review","claude-cli","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/prompt.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:28.968595Z","id":"9d7b7a03bde2489160cd1a2aa01a668a6186e65f7454ec3bf79e902eb074e800","body":{"detail":"AgentRequest.image carries the first comment's PNG clip and the Messages API backend sends it as an image block before the text (spec section 3.6), but the text never mentions it, so the model has to guess what the picture is. One line under the first comment when a clip is present ('The image shows the region this comment is anchored on.') ties them together; the claude -p backend sends no image, so the line belongs only when the request carries one.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":114},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"861b735f905659c696c9ca336459debd260b8b34e878cc799c78e21dd11d952c"},"summary":"The change prompt does not say that an attached image is the first comment's clip","tags":["review","prompt","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/prompt.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:28.968682Z","id":"e5dc33c948f91302fb4934ba397906d5c58529f1df3551eeab125afb276af332","body":{"detail":"Spec section 8 says comment text and documents go in the prompt as JSON strings. The anchor's quote is page text, which can include the person's documents or other apps' data rendered on the page, and a newline in it can forge a 'Comment:' line or a new section. Quoting the whole line where it is written (prompt.dart:119, jsonEncode(c.anchorLine)) keeps the property in one place with its test; leaving it to lib/agent/loop.dart spreads it across two files. test/agent/prompt_test.dart:176 pins the unquoted form and changes with it; add a case with a newline and 'Comment:' in the anchor.","kind":"comment","references":"b041ea0214dec031a8df84775b2ec9e7cea7beb5e8eef5ad12882ffaba34a5b2","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"72d1d0918b41b8390e360792f83ec31640d348c6f9cf350c9e988e603fd4dee8"},"summary":"Review: fix this in PromptBuilder now, not in the feedback worker","tags":["review","security","prompt","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_result.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:11:28.968758Z","id":"13b1ee98d89d02c5beac97e8eb62d457ca1a77beaa463a04fe5e03cfd08abf53","body":{"detail":"validateResult is the gate before anything is published, and the code that applies a result does not exist yet. Refusing (1) the same path twice in files, (2) a path both in files and in removed, and (3) an edit on a path in removed, each with a named reason, lets the one retry fix them and leaves the applier a single meaning to implement. Two edits on the same path stay allowed: they apply in order.","kind":"comment","references":"1d76d70ec363a2b25c56d46a32ab274f275e2b1a62ef7c55878a3680785520bb","span":{"start":{"line":221},"end":{"line":240},"content_hash":"3199a4dbb21944535df116037febfe986383332e2f390bd23376fd97c4286edc"},"summary":"Review: refuse these in validateResult now","tags":["review","validation","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:12:10.549213Z","id":"c722498e8c28082955b686e9e128bd55735af2e14e12ba62f519521ba8367b34","body":{"detail":"MessagesApiBackend.run sends one request and throws AgentError(retryable: true) on 408/429/5xx (line 143), on a timeout and on an IOException. Nothing in lib/agent reads AgentError.retryable: the change flow in docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app.md (Task F4b, 'backend error replies with the reason and acks') turns any backend error into a 'Couldn't make that change' reply. A brief 529 overload on the phone therefore fails the person's change outright, where the official SDKs retry twice with backoff.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":16},"content_hash":"4790ee6a638e70b8996da7eeed0be8340a3929e8ea7f8a9efc28b2bb9444f1e8"},"suggested_fix":"Retry once or twice on retryable errors with backoff, honouring the retry-after header, either here (with an injected delay so tests stay deterministic) or in AgentLoop before replying.","summary":"A retryable Messages API failure (429, 529, 5xx, timeout, unreachable) is never retried","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:12:10.549410Z","id":"2ab7d46469be3dfc22538fa516e427a2d6d35342a609edd1db5f4b3237a5f93e","body":{"detail":"A new app's whole index.html travels inside one JSON string; at about 3-4 characters per token, 16000 output tokens (thinking included) is roughly 50 KB of result. A larger app stops with stop_reason max_tokens, which run() reports as the non-retryable 'The result was too long' (line 170). maxResultBytes in apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_result.dart is 8 MiB, so the two limits disagree by two orders of magnitude. Raising max_tokens past about 16000 needs streaming to stay under HTTP timeouts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":29},"content_hash":"7ee51ed7d3fafff2c82f26e2446099a8fdb900be72907249ae3a01a29c6a2a22"},"suggested_fix":"Stream the response (SSE) and raise max_tokens (Haiku 5.5 allows 128K), or tell the model the output budget in system.md so it prefers edits and compact apps.","summary":"max_tokens 16000 caps a result far below what validateResult allows (8 MiB)","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:12:10.549536Z","id":"434383b69743e08280d24834604909326725b112a2a6bdc0e3790b9a27282c8a","body":{"detail":"The request body is exactly the one docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app.md gives for Task F5, with no anthropic-beta header and no fallbacks parameter. The default model claude-haiku-5-5 has no server-side fallback, so a refusal is final and run() throws a non-retryable AgentError naming its category. claude-sonnet-5-5 and claude-opus-5-5, offered in settings, accept fallbacks: \"default\" with the server-side-fallback-2026-07-01 beta header, which would re-run a declined request on another model inside the same call.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":163},"end":{"line":168},"content_hash":"a75c696ef485d8913e7d7a6104527cbdbfa2c80f8fb272077040142b73ca0f4f"},"summary":"Server-side refusal fallbacks (the fallbacks request parameter) are not sent","tags":["revisit:refusals are seen in practice with claude-sonnet-5-5 or claude-opus-5-5 selected","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:13:14.131391Z","id":"44916c1880a906d1c1d8eae7f9677fd30f29619b3a2cfb624f6e2c6499698a37","body":{"detail":"ClaudeCliBackend takes its own CliProcessStarter (a function returning dart:io's Process) instead of the ProcessStarter interface in lib/daemon/process.dart. That interface's RunningProcess exposes no stdin or stdout, and IoProcessStarter closes stdin, discards stdout and starts the child without the parent's environment; claude needs the request on stdin, its JSON on stdout, and the person's login from the parent's environment. A distinct name also avoids an import clash where both are used (the app wiring).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":26},"content_hash":"0916b94c85eeca896f70c48b77b604ecfe96a4c32760278b7c627e1184423bac"},"summary":"Reuse ProcessStarter from lib/daemon/process.dart for starting claude","tags":["revisit:lib/daemon/process.dart gains stdin, stdout and an inherit-environment option","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:13:14.131481Z","id":"e273e8eaabc463a35cc9b4690718c5036f4b2fcce1c00a0323b974abe8478ff8","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 3.6 sets the default model to claude-haiku-5-5 at effort low for both backends, and MessagesApiBackend sends output_config.effort low. The argument list here follows the plan's exact list (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app.md, Task F6), which has no --effort, and AgentRequest carries no effort; claude --help lists --effort <low|medium|high|xhigh|max>. The two backends therefore differ in speed and cost for the same request, which matters for the say-to-usable timing measured in the live runs. Options: append '--effort', 'low' here, or add an effort field to AgentRequest (lib/agent/request.dart) that both backends pass on.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":67},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"2e251c1336b417214534e10c063cc606d6efd62af01b365bd6d6cdad009b4ff0"},"summary":"claude -p runs at the CLI's default effort, not effort low","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:13:14.131517Z","id":"479b131e33372b62ac10b698c04caeea072f4a82a5140e8e241f085cfe06e53b","body":{"detail":"Each run makes its own directory under scratch (createTemp 'run-'), writes system.md there, runs claude in it and removes it afterwards. One shared <scratch>/system.md would be overwritten by a second run started while the first is still running (a new app while a change runs), so the first could read the other's prompt.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"66ff4cfa9bfe18fa4ea7efab98e047bc688178b4cf8730791031ec0ec045739b"},"summary":"Write the system prompt to <scratch>/system.md and run claude in scratch itself","tags":["revisit:the backend is guaranteed to run one request at a time","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:13:14.131548Z","id":"c0e2029b29ada96cc9190859b28acd1086f7b6296976c4dc7ccd3b777aa502c4","body":{"detail":"Any JSON output with is_error true becomes AgentError(retryable: false), whatever its subtype or cause, so a transient API overload or rate limit seen through claude -p is not retried, while MessagesApiBackend marks 429/529/5xx retryable. The CLI's JSON does not separate transient from permanent failures in a field this code reads; a non-zero exit without JSON is likewise not retryable. Revisit when the live runs show which subtypes and messages claude prints for transient failures.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":210},"end":{"line":217},"content_hash":"3af0fc69cd6755e39f64f189e6b34a32913a6c4b4f83d16d782825224d07b09d"},"summary":"An is_error result from claude is never retryable","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:15:50.982513Z","id":"1e562988cb91771336261f5516b0bbaf5e8c7c71a8ec6baa0e659631b9318803","body":{"detail":"The HTTP status and the retry-after header are only visible here. The official SDKs retry the same failures run() already marks retryable (408, 429, 5xx including 529, and connection errors) twice with backoff, honouring retry-after. AgentLoop's one retry (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 3.6, Retries) is a different thing: it changes the request, naming the validation failure and asking for full files. The claude -p backend (lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart) already gets the CLI's own API retries, so a loop-level transport retry would only duplicate them there. Shape: up to 2 retries on 408, 429, 5xx and on a connection error before any response arrives; delay = retry-after seconds when present (capped, for example at 20 s), else 1 s then 2 s; delays through an injected constructor parameter (Future<void> Function(Duration) delay, default Future.delayed) so tests assert the delays without waiting. No retry after a timeout (the 5 minutes at line 23 are already spent), after another 4xx, a refusal or max_tokens. The AgentError then means the retries are exhausted. Requirement for lib/agent/loop.dart (plan Task F4b, not yet written): never re-send a request because AgentError.retryable is true; a backend AgentError goes straight to the 'Couldn't make that change: <reason>' reply for a change, or to the New sheet's reason with Retry for a new app, so waits do not multiply.","kind":"comment","references":"c722498e8c28082955b686e9e128bd55735af2e14e12ba62f519521ba8367b34","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":16},"content_hash":"4790ee6a638e70b8996da7eeed0be8340a3929e8ea7f8a9efc28b2bb9444f1e8"},"summary":"Review: the transport retry belongs in MessagesApiBackend, not in AgentLoop","tags":["review","retries","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:15:50.982624Z","id":"958fbc567c70bd3a1e0ab5ef14c2c64b40ad420d0251dda54733ea303c48b239","body":{"detail":"16000 is the documented safe value for a non-streaming request: the SDKs refuse non-streaming requests above about 21K max_tokens (their 10-minute expected-time rule), and a non-streaming response sends no bytes until it is complete, which idle-connection timeouts on mobile networks can cut. Streaming would not shorten say-to-usable: validateResult and createArtifact need the whole JSON. It would only let the New sheet show progress, at the cost of an SSE parser. A single-file app usable within seconds is a few thousand to about ten thousand output tokens (an index.html of roughly 10-40 KB, JSON-escaped, with little thinking at effort low); a result that needs more than 16000 tokens already takes too long for the say-to-usable goal. So for v1: keep 16000 non-streaming and the non-retryable 'too long' error (a retry asking for full files would be longer still), and have assets/prompt/system.md tell the model to keep index.html compact and to answer changes with edits rather than whole files. maxResultBytes (8 MiB, lib/agent/edit_result.dart) guards what the daemon accepts and need not match the model's output cap. Revisit streaming with a higher cap if the live runs' timings show max_tokens stops, or when the New sheet wants a progress indicator. Note: with claude-opus-5-5 or claude-sonnet-5-5 selected in settings, 16000 output tokens take longer than on Haiku and can approach the 5-minute timeout at line 23; the SDKs default to 10 minutes.","kind":"comment","references":"2ab7d46469be3dfc22538fa516e427a2d6d35342a609edd1db5f4b3237a5f93e","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":29},"content_hash":"7ee51ed7d3fafff2c82f26e2446099a8fdb900be72907249ae3a01a29c6a2a22"},"summary":"Review: keep max_tokens 16000 without streaming for v1, and keep results small through the prompt","tags":["review","revisit:the live runs' timings record a stop_reason max_tokens, or the New sheet gains a progress indicator","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:15:50.982662Z","id":"7f80e0784e978bf225d1a4054ac8e4e8c7f746524cc44c7d935b0ce7c0b40272","body":{"detail":"The HTTP log line has status, time and request-id only. Whether the cached system block (line 57) is actually read is visible only in usage.cache_read_input_tokens; a zero across consecutive runs means something in the system prompt varies. Output tokens next to the time show how close a result came to max_tokens (line 29). These are counts, not content, so they are safe in the log.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":110},"end":{"line":113},"content_hash":"8272b4cfcceab7930a8a6f6f419919fb9416d1856b481e1c0e34ae794b4abc16"},"summary":"Log the response's usage (input, output, cache read and cache write tokens) and stop_reason","tags":["review","observability","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:15:50.982724Z","id":"002ae17ab17fdecf487b1024917d1317cc2d739110c9bde0a84c40bd2895af0d","body":{"detail":"Without req.contentLength, dart:io sends the body with chunked transfer encoding. Some proxies (an injectable base URL can point through one) refuse or buffer chunked requests; the body is already fully encoded, so encoding it once into a variable and setting contentLength to its length costs nothing.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":105},"end":{"line":105},"content_hash":"68d12f481cd3583c756324594145e4fe66d5ec15b17086d6f43738c1943c5390"},"summary":"Set the request's contentLength before writing the body","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_result.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:15:54.617666Z","id":"39289ce786bf30acf7884d9410978bd6d0f670f80c05f4cb73ef7fec83bc3fe6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d03c23b7","summary":"validateResult applies the daemon's segments/segment_ok rule (crates/clax-core/src/db.rs) to collection/doc_id via _checkDocPath: charset, . and .., 200-byte segments, 1000-byte paths, 16 segments. Test: 'db paths follow the daemon's segment rule' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/edit_result_test.dart, a table of accepted and refused cases drawn from the Rust rule. `flutter test test/agent/edit_result_test.dart test/agent/prompt_test.dart` (apps/clax_app): +23, All tests passed; the same tests against the fd9a5db4 sources: +18 -5.","supersedes":"02408d6b80a7ca649671c41c4a511cca863557e94ffc752a5601f0aa5941d775","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/prompt.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:15:54.617901Z","id":"e2e2693720f3a8c12b7a746b9942935bacd5214449a90cec90624d11f667f633","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d03c23b7","summary":"PromptBuilder.change writes the anchor line as jsonEncode(anchorLine). Test: 'the anchor line is JSON-quoted, so page text cannot break out' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/prompt_test.dart. `flutter test test/agent/edit_result_test.dart test/agent/prompt_test.dart` (apps/clax_app): +23, All tests passed; the same tests against the fd9a5db4 sources: +18 -5.","supersedes":"b041ea0214dec031a8df84775b2ec9e7cea7beb5e8eef5ad12882ffaba34a5b2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_result.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:15:54.618033Z","id":"a125466d00e596993aeb22765e44b6d794158655e49108cde00b5251871f8bb4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d03c23b7","summary":"validateResult refuses a path written twice in files, a path both written and removed, and a path both edited and removed; cases in validation_refuses_hostile_results (apps/clax_app/test/agent/edit_result_test.dart). `flutter test test/agent/edit_result_test.dart test/agent/prompt_test.dart` (apps/clax_app): +23, All tests passed; the same tests against the fd9a5db4 sources: +18 -5.","supersedes":"1d76d70ec363a2b25c56d46a32ab274f275e2b1a62ef7c55878a3680785520bb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_result.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:15:54.618149Z","id":"94bfed50effe7b85d47b4208f4490274a0ddb69ebe941b4caca595fac4b90dcd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d03c23b7","summary":"_checkPath refuses U+0000-U+001F and U+007F-U+009F (char::is_control) and U+2028/U+2029, as check_path in crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs; cases for U+0080, U+0085, U+009F, U+2028, U+2029 and a trailing slash in validation_refuses_hostile_results. `flutter test test/agent/edit_result_test.dart test/agent/prompt_test.dart` (apps/clax_app): +23, All tests passed; the same tests against the fd9a5db4 sources: +18 -5.","supersedes":"5f0eadcd4a81e91d233c2802156851d44716a1dd32c303f11ab8589d44296b9a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/prompt.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:15:54.618372Z","id":"5348a3e17691b0c1dccf47042c4e45f0c593855dfb017d898de9e6cc9812f53c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d03c23b7","summary":"When the first comment carries a clip, PromptBuilder.change says under it that the attached image is comment 1's clip; CommentContext.clip's doc says to set it only when the backend sends AgentRequest.image. Test: 'a clip on the first comment is named as the attached image' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/prompt_test.dart. `flutter test test/agent/edit_result_test.dart test/agent/prompt_test.dart` (apps/clax_app): +23, All tests passed; the same tests against the fd9a5db4 sources: +18 -5.","supersedes":"9d7b7a03bde2489160cd1a2aa01a668a6186e65f7454ec3bf79e902eb074e800","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:18:13.071752Z","id":"29643c55d9b1555ea84b3cc6c7d2ab53981360fb5b33377b8c1154ab28da26d5","body":{"kind":"comment","ref":"git:47b961fc","references":"958fbc567c70bd3a1e0ab5ef14c2c64b40ad420d0251dda54733ea303c48b239","summary":"apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/system.md now states the budget (about 16000 output tokens, roughly 40 KB), asks for a compact self-contained index.html with no large data blobs, embedded images or pasted libraries, and asks for changes as minimal edits, not whole-file rewrites. Test 'system.md states the output budget the Messages API backend sends…' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/prompt_test.dart ties the stated number to MessagesApiBackend.maxTokens. flutter test test/agent/prompt_test.dart test/agent/edit_result_test.dart: +24, all passed; scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh --check: exit 0.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:18:56.605060Z","id":"3983bcc5cbc47f23696ac51e3c8c283fa08bbc31814d21015c307b12ad0fdf48","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:01203e52","summary":"MessagesApiBackend.run now retries 408, 429, 5xx and connection failures up to 2 times (retry-after capped at 20 s, else 1 s then 2 s, delay injected) and never after a timeout, other 4xx, refusal or max_tokens. flutter test test/agent/messages_api_backend_test.dart: 36 passed, including 'HTTP 529 is retried twice, 1 s then 2 s', 'retry-after sets the delay, capped at 20 s', 'a server that never answers times out, without a retry', 'HTTP 400 is not retried'.","supersedes":"c722498e8c28082955b686e9e128bd55735af2e14e12ba62f519521ba8367b34","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:18:56.605260Z","id":"4186aa8160fe576e4d67078701a3787afc231882afb12ef095e8e5104e2cec47","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:01203e52","summary":"_parse logs stop_reason and input, output, cache_read and cache_creation token counts, redacted like every other line. Test 'logs the stop reason and the usage counts' passes (36 of 36 in test/agent/messages_api_backend_test.dart).","supersedes":"7f80e0784e978bf225d1a4054ac8e4e8c7f746524cc44c7d935b0ce7c0b40272","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:18:56.605394Z","id":"3ae5dbdb883a381001e0861dccf143e9d205aa9981fab5d422eee2bdf5d245e3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:01203e52","summary":"The body is encoded once per run and _send sets contentLength to its length. Test 'the body is sent with a content-length, not chunked' asserts no transfer-encoding and a content-length equal to the body's UTF-8 length; it passes.","supersedes":"002ae17ab17fdecf487b1024917d1317cc2d739110c9bde0a84c40bd2895af0d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:19:58.515472Z","id":"88999173016cbbdcf427408b32f7281790ffab41aeca2a493cf3e61c1a4938a8","body":{"detail":"Failure: on a Mac whose ~/.claude has hooks (SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit, Stop), installed plugins or a ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md, every app generation runs those hooks in the run directory, loads the plugins' skills and agents, and sends CLAUDE.md and auto-memory into the request, changing the output and adding latency. --strict-mcp-config only drops MCP servers, and --system-prompt-file replaces the system prompt but not the CLAUDE.md context. claude 2.1.296's `--safe-mode` disables CLAUDE.md, skills, installed plugins, hooks, MCP servers, custom agents and output styles while 'Auth, model selection, built-in tools and plugins, and permissions work normally' (claude -p --help). `--bare` is not usable here: it never reads OAuth or the keychain ('Anthropic auth is strictly ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or apiKeyHelper'), so a person signed in with their Claude login, the reason this backend exists (spec section 3.6), would fail to authenticate.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":67},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"2e251c1336b417214534e10c063cc606d6efd62af01b365bd6d6cdad009b4ff0"},"suggested_fix":"Append '--safe-mode' to arguments() and to the argument-order test in apps/clax_app/test/agent/claude_cli_backend_test.dart.","summary":"claude -p loads the person's hooks, plugins, skills, CLAUDE.md and auto-memory","tags":["review","claude-cli","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:19:58.515564Z","id":"c4bf4b2d69f7e7a0552df3a24a6c5b13af9e7da011902eb569f63f21a2acbd38","body":{"detail":"startWithParentEnvironment passes the whole parent environment. An app launched by `flutter run` from inside a Claude Code session carries CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION, CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_SOCKET/TOKEN, CLAUDE_PID, CLAUDE_EFFORT and CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA (all present in such a shell's env); the child claude then reads itself as a child of that session, may talk to its messaging socket, and CLAUDE_EFFORT can change the effort. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in the environment also switches claude from the person's login to API-key billing. Dropping CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_*, CLAUDE_PID, CLAUDE_EFFORT and CLAUDE_PLUGIN_* (keeping HOME, PATH, USER, TMPDIR and the rest) keeps the login and avoids the coupling; a starter test can assert the filtered map.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":14},"end":{"line":26},"content_hash":"14f74c7f2db64ef6532e910b76ffd24fdfa98ecceb2559adbc3fedc6a3b3a83b"},"summary":"The child inherits CLAUDECODE and CLAUDE_CODE_* session variables when the app is started from a Claude Code session","tags":["review","claude-cli","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:19:58.515599Z","id":"28e56f5742421fc192016f6156f0c551edd4059c58d6bbae91ea2c9fd89ec9c6","body":{"detail":"run() has no cancellation input and AgentBackend (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/backend.dart) has no cancel, so the making screen's Cancel (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md line 358) can only abandon the Future: the claude process keeps running, spending the person's quota, until it finishes or the timeout kills it. A cancel signal (a Future or token passed to run) that calls _kill would close this; it touches the interface owned by lib/agent/backend.dart and the loop that calls it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":147},"content_hash":"420b92adf598e42542358c3bc4d1256e6dec0adca47ae88faa86153987321f22"},"summary":"Nothing can stop a running claude before its 300 s timeout","tags":["review","claude-cli","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:19:58.515629Z","id":"bd295e4e964f3ad546a80d780f186c492bdc86a5a15d7838c377b102947a02ac","body":{"detail":"A GUI app gets launchd's PATH (/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin), so the PATH search never reaches /opt/homebrew/bin or /usr/local/bin; only ~/.local/bin/claude (the native installer) is found without the settings override. Adding /opt/homebrew/bin/claude and /usr/local/bin/claude after ~/.local/bin/claude covers the Homebrew and npm-global installs.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":89},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"7689a2830f712d639336dd77f1f9d0f7ee42bc2d98cb14d2556c267ca7cbfdfd"},"summary":"find misses Homebrew's claude when the app is opened from Finder","tags":["review","claude-cli","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:19:58.515955Z","id":"c4e88109e9443918d9df8b0c9da66296da6169ba1735b0d79ddc006cac7f529b","body":{"detail":"claude -p --help lists `--effort <level>` (low, medium, high, xhigh, max), and the binary's own argument table carries it. Spec section 3.6 and section 12 D-2 set effort low for both backends, so this needs no owner decision and no AgentRequest field: arguments() should append '--effort', 'low', with the argument-order test updated. Live check: a parent CLAUDE_EFFORT variable must not override the flag (see the environment concern on lines 14-26).","kind":"comment","references":"e273e8eaabc463a35cc9b4690718c5036f4b2fcce1c00a0323b974abe8478ff8","summary":"--effort exists in claude 2.1.296 and the spec already fixes the value: append '--effort', 'low'","tags":["review","claude-cli","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_schema.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:19:58.516001Z","id":"1641a6efee3ab253bb52893f783e921e0ccc06fda429d3d28f67cd347925d624","body":{"detail":"In the binary's CLI startup path the parsed --json-schema becomes the StructuredOutput tool and is appended to the already-resolved tool list (`Hs=M,en=[...en,M]`, logged as tengu_structured_output_enabled), and requiresStructuredOutput is set when that list contains it; nothing there consults --tools. --system-prompt-file is also a real (unlisted in --help) option: the binary's option table has `--system-prompt-file <file>  Read system prompt from a file`. The live run must still confirm, with the exact argument list of ClaudeCliBackend.arguments plus --safe-mode and --effort low and the person's OAuth login: exit 0, is_error false, `structured_output` an object that EditResult.fromJson accepts; that no hook ran (e.g. with --debug-file, no hook execution lines); and that the time to result fits the say-to-usable budget.","kind":"comment","references":"0f5e9d556f451b80d34ae63ddb6a29c1833e998e32330255becffb5eff044536","summary":"In claude 2.1.296 the --json-schema tool is appended after the --tools selection, so it most likely survives --tools \"\"","tags":["review","claude-cli","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:26:17.630254Z","id":"40122112eec3ca67ea2488c1e36386f3ed1b50c9d3aa17a304cd6ded18fa0d50","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4b7c271c","summary":"ClaudeCliBackend.arguments ends with --safe-mode (not --bare, which would not read the Claude login); test 'passes the arguments in order…' asserts it. flutter test test/agent/claude_cli_backend_test.dart (in apps/clax_app): +23, all passed","supersedes":"88999173016cbbdcf427408b32f7281790ffab41aeca2a493cf3e61c1a4938a8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:26:17.630477Z","id":"c0eaa6eeada20b4e2432c937cff017971f405d713e805661f1dda69963c05c99","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4b7c271c","summary":"ClaudeCliBackend.arguments passes '--effort', 'low' (ClaudeCliBackend.effort) after --model, as reply c4e88109 states the spec fixes; test 'passes the arguments in order…' asserts it. flutter test test/agent/claude_cli_backend_test.dart (in apps/clax_app): +23, all passed","supersedes":"e273e8eaabc463a35cc9b4690718c5036f4b2fcce1c00a0323b974abe8478ff8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:26:17.630625Z","id":"a96fd3daa9af527994a7b674a2e86f7ae55a8f41ef20086ae47bccbf02c50581","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4b7c271c","summary":"claudeEnvironment drops CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_* (except CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, a login method), CLAUDE_PID, CLAUDE_EFFORT, CLAUDE_PLUGIN_* and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, and the starter gets exactly that map (includeParentEnvironment false). Test 'the child gets the parent environment without Claude Code session variables or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY' checks the map passed and the fixture's logged env. flutter test test/agent/claude_cli_backend_test.dart (in apps/clax_app): +23, all passed","supersedes":"c4bf4b2d69f7e7a0552df3a24a6c5b13af9e7da011902eb569f63f21a2acbd38","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:26:17.630770Z","id":"d8492bc60771c972ff3bf6a6aee29f9bb6302b3d8895f6470435274781f4cb0f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4b7c271c","summary":"AgentRequest.cancelled (lib/agent/request.dart) is honoured by both backends through CancelWatch (lib/agent/backend.dart) and ends in AgentError.cancelled (kind AgentErrorKind.cancelled, not retryable). ClaudeCliBackend sends SIGTERM, waits killGrace, then SIGKILL; MessagesApiBackend aborts the request and sends no retry. Tests: 'cancelling a running claude terminates it…', 'a request cancelled before the run starts no process' (claude_cli_backend_test.dart); 'cancelling while the API has not answered aborts the request…', 'cancelling during the wait before a retry sends no retry', 'a request cancelled before the run sends nothing' (messages_api_backend_test.dart). flutter test test/agent: +87, all passed.","supersedes":"28e56f5742421fc192016f6156f0c551edd4059c58d6bbae91ea2c9fd89ec9c6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:26:17.630913Z","id":"3bd498d12b0eaad589055ea1a39f06b8820db5f0065d0418851bb1b676fac9fa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4b7c271c","summary":"find looks in ClaudeCliBackend.fallbackDirs after PATH: ~/.local/bin, /opt/homebrew/bin, /usr/local/bin. Test 'find falls back to Homebrew after ~/.local/bin'. flutter test test/agent/claude_cli_backend_test.dart (in apps/clax_app): +23, all passed","supersedes":"bd295e4e964f3ad546a80d780f186c492bdc86a5a15d7838c377b102947a02ac","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:27:53.530581Z","id":"a07882610e87b95e960e1f3f8ab72ac09c5fe80e25ee13afed457a8c9747829e","body":{"detail":"The prefix rule removes CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK, CLAUDE_CODE_USE_VERTEX, CLAUDE_CODE_USE_FOUNDRY, CLAUDE_CODE_SKIP_BEDROCK_AUTH/CLAUDE_CODE_SKIP_VERTEX_AUTH and similar settings along with the session variables, so a person whose claude works through a third-party provider configured in the environment (an app started from their shell) gets a claude that falls back to the Anthropic login and fails. It also drops ANTHROPIC_API_KEY but keeps ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, which equally replaces the person's login. An app opened from the Finder has neither, so the effect is limited to apps started from a terminal. Narrower rule: drop the session variables by name (CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_PID, CLAUDE_EFFORT, CLAUDE_PLUGIN_*, CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_*, CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION, CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_*, CLAUDE_CODE_EXECPATH, CLAUDE_CODE_SSE_PORT, CLAUDE_CODE_SIMPLE, CLAUDE_CODE_SAFE_MODE) and keep CLAUDE_CODE_USE_*; decide ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN the same way as ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. The test in apps/clax_app/test/agent/claude_cli_backend_test.dart ('the child gets the parent environment without Claude Code session variables…') would add a kept CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":41},"end":{"line":52},"content_hash":"270154917116d414d765c7d0060d62af736f414aebb98c1eef09fd7ce534def3"},"summary":"claudeEnvironment drops every CLAUDE_CODE_* variable, including provider and auth configuration","tags":["review","claude-cli","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:29:29.595839Z","id":"b958c92a994a5c0f10c9a2dd38d73e4cc85bf2b71e52f2ac56c0e326e11cc354","body":{"detail":"ClaudeCliBackend takes its own CliProcessStarter (a function returning dart:io's Process, given an exact environment) instead of the ProcessStarter interface in lib/daemon/process.dart. That interface's RunningProcess exposes no stdin or stdout, and IoProcessStarter closes stdin and discards stdout; claude needs the request on stdin and prints its JSON on stdout. A distinct name also avoids an import clash where both are used (the app wiring).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":11},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"b4a99e24447e4c6b29d50b6e523303084fda59048cd5268cf337bbb18997d362"},"summary":"Reuse ProcessStarter from lib/daemon/process.dart for starting claude","supersedes":"44916c1880a906d1c1d8eae7f9677fd30f29619b3a2cfb624f6e2c6499698a37","tags":["revisit:lib/daemon/process.dart gains stdin and stdout","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:29:29.596129Z","id":"e297629f6d5591f60a59f2ac09943437f161669cdbd45e8e91d9fe8c33422b04","body":{"detail":"Each run makes its own directory under scratch (createTemp 'run-'), writes system.md there, runs claude in it and removes it afterwards. One shared <scratch>/system.md would be overwritten by a second run started while the first is still running (a new app while a change runs), so the first could read the other's prompt.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":196},"end":{"line":231},"content_hash":"46b3ec5bc4df857d2b1d61c1d463d0929e228a0158899bbc5569c8d1f22c0028"},"summary":"Write the system prompt to <scratch>/system.md and run claude in scratch itself","supersedes":"479b131e33372b62ac10b698c04caeea072f4a82a5140e8e241f085cfe06e53b","tags":["revisit:the backend is guaranteed to run one request at a time","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:29:29.596328Z","id":"8e831ac8196dcbf82d831a10ba19985dc6f99777d53197fac47e5342b61f8a0c","body":{"detail":"Any JSON output with is_error true becomes AgentError(retryable: false), whatever its subtype or cause, so a transient API overload or rate limit seen through claude -p is not retried, while MessagesApiBackend marks 429/529/5xx retryable. The CLI's JSON does not separate transient from permanent failures in a field this code reads; a non-zero exit without JSON is likewise not retryable. Revisit when the live runs show which subtypes and messages claude prints for transient failures.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":307},"end":{"line":318},"content_hash":"c26f3dc33fa5a6763287a75633e6531149cb4a7019a992b2dfc39ce828e85423"},"summary":"An is_error result from claude is never retryable","supersedes":"c0e2029b29ada96cc9190859b28acd1086f7b6296976c4dc7ccd3b777aa502c4","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:29:29.596481Z","id":"8fb5295094baa08d607f531272ba65433d3ed78979c56acf6ea3a531bc23732c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5131103c","summary":"claudeEnvironment now drops droppedSessionVariables by name (CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_PID, CLAUDE_EFFORT, CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT, CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION, CLAUDE_CODE_EXECPATH, CLAUDE_CODE_SSE_PORT, CLAUDE_CODE_SIMPLE, CLAUDE_CODE_SAFE_MODE, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN) and the prefixes CLAUDE_PLUGIN_, CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_, CLAUDE_CODE_MESSAGING_; CLAUDE_CODE_USE_*, CLAUDE_CODE_SKIP_*_AUTH, CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and the rest are kept. Both Anthropic keys are dropped, documented on claudeEnvironment: this backend runs on the Claude login, the Messages API backend on a key. Test 'the child gets the parent environment without the variables of a parent Claude Code session or an API key, keeping provider and auth settings' asserts the kept and dropped sets in the starter's map and the child's env. flutter test test/agent/{claude_cli_backend,messages_api_backend,edit_result,prompt}_test.dart (apps/clax_app): +87, all passed.","supersedes":"a07882610e87b95e960e1f3f8ab72ac09c5fe80e25ee13afed457a8c9747829e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:34:08.648259Z","id":"17992740481617c91a095b3ddf4f0ce703379cb6c25b83e8b1071ec2436a175b","body":{"detail":"AgentLoop sets CommentContext.clip and AgentRequest.image only for backends named in imageBackends (messages-api, scripted); claude-cli runs with tools off and sends no image. A new backend that takes images gets no clip until it is added here. A member on AgentBackend (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/backend.dart), for example `bool get sendsImage`, would let each backend say so itself; AgentLoop's sendsImage constructor parameter is the seam until then.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"056cd14e2264c1f739187ed9df6039b05adb7ef287aa65f6d90b77311cfdbc32"},"summary":"Whether a backend sends AgentRequest.image is decided by its name","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:34:08.648363Z","id":"8824e56f4ff6ea1fee16a669a79e84b920ea5bb0fecee574d45a7a0ce79c4f54","body":{"detail":"newApp creates the artifact, then applies the result's db operations; when batchDocs refuses them the refusal is only logged and the artifact ID is returned, so the person gets an app without the data it was built to start with and no message. Throwing instead would leave an artifact the New sheet's Retry would duplicate. A returned warning (for example a record with the ID and a note) would let the UI say it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":164},"end":{"line":172},"content_hash":"399aaf3ac4e1a9f9c0b9d2aeb40d7672ee1b1c53ebcacdf4642b16260714618d"},"summary":"A new app whose starting documents are refused is returned without telling the caller","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:34:08.648406Z","id":"05e6a51b1c33c5b9cf8234762fba49d2fa264448f28b25dc0fd63bfb499d8af7","body":{"detail":"change publishes the new version first and applies the result's db operations after it. When batchDocs refuses them, the reply names the refusal (\"Its data wasn't changed: …\") and the thread is resolved as the result asked, but the landed page may read documents in the new shape that were never migrated. Applying the documents before the publish moves the risk to the old page reading migrated documents; neither order is atomic over the daemon API.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":345},"end":{"line":355},"content_hash":"50db6bb8249d747f804d8984e3aa74bbd5df9b2ee417e19dd4af646d5a5bef60"},"summary":"A change whose document migration is refused has already published the code that expects it","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:34:08.648439Z","id":"00cc95d2374aad965d4bfde6e7d7917f5f39e930e9d323932cbd629549962f1b","body":{"detail":"_applyDb reads each distinct document path once and pins every write to that path to the version it read. A result with two writes to one existing document (for example set then update) sends the same if_version twice; if the daemon checks each write of a docs:batch against the document as the earlier writes left it, the second is a conflict and the whole batch is refused. Untested against the real daemon.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":447},"end":{"line":465},"content_hash":"ef6c465ab8a5754efeac0dc63786185156d1ea31c3019a820ba1216febadd599"},"summary":"Several writes to one document in one result all carry its version from before the batch","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:34:08.648476Z","id":"03d18a782e9ffe63e0de76fe2c94f26e2a0b03b3e6ee00a703ad49c2b8d0d431","body":{"detail":"ThreadView.stranded does not name the session the feedback was sent to, so recovery re-runs any open, acknowledged, unanswered thread in the home. In the app's own CLAX_HOME only the app session takes feedback, so this holds; a home shared with other harness sessions would have the app run their threads. A stranded thread whose addressed_in names a version created at or after its last viewer comment (comparing created_at strings parsed as RFC 3339, millisecond precision from the daemon) gets the reply 'Made this change in version N.' instead of a second run; a comment and an unrelated version in the same millisecond would be misread.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":225},"end":{"line":262},"content_hash":"02229ec54653c430b1817fe80675f10288e4079ee2ff659977d48b1240d490f0"},"summary":"Recovery re-runs stranded threads of every session, and judges a landed change by timestamps","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:34:08.648507Z","id":"b50cd0117d003f8487984b4d6ee76078eec3c8309df82378e3c6c78b912371d2","body":{"detail":"_drain passes the session ID current when the change starts. If the worker registers again mid-change (a daemon restart that made a new session row), the change's ackFeedback goes to the old session and fails with unknown_session, which is logged and ignored. The app session's wait-tier feedback is acknowledged at hand-over (crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:321-328), so nothing is lost today; a tier that waits for the explicit ack would need the current session here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":186},"end":{"line":193},"content_hash":"2a7c1e3e48d5997ce167779d1e52c6239bdcbfdafd1e52233c6bd8e4d3dfc70f"},"summary":"A change acknowledges to the session it started under, even after a re-registration","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:40:08.917667Z","id":"d99e02cbb9a4354a4f5ccaf1ffadbdf2e5a23bec5cf2ea457c0bab6d52e286a4","body":{"detail":"Failure: an EditResult whose db list names one document twice, for example [set runs/r1, update runs/r1], makes _applyDb send a docs:batch that addresses runs/r1 twice; Store::doc_batch refuses any batch that addresses a document more than once (crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs:960-972, \"a batch addresses each document at most once\"), so every write of the result is dropped. In newApp the refusal is only logged (loop.dart:166-172) and the app opens without its seed data; in change the version is already published, the reply gains \"(Its data wasn't changed: ...)\" and the thread is still resolved. This confirms 00cc95d2. Fix: refuse such a result in validation (ResultInvalid naming the document), so the existing one retry asks the model again before anything is created or published; a test with a duplicate path pins it.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":445},"end":{"line":465},"content_hash":"bdc7a0afb8928d66053b422d2d905e624e65146d2ecfbe63b027b4d97ca6d4d8"},"summary":"A result with two db writes to one document is refused whole by the daemon","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:40:08.918073Z","id":"2a312a4c496c2676a21964310902c8cfcb624850e95d75db092d1b345a34e004","body":{"detail":"The change prompt (PromptBuilder.change, apps/clax_app/lib/agent/prompt.dart:85-145) carries the app's files, the comments and the other apps' summaries, but nothing of the app's own documents, while it and assets/prompt/system.md:71-74 tell the model to migrate with db operations when a shape changes. A migration written blind can only guess values: a set of a document path the code names (for example settings/main) replaces what the person stored, and _applyDb (loop.dart:447-465) reads that document's version and pins the write to it, so the daemon's conflict check never stops it. This works against the 'changes land with data kept' promise. Options: give the change prompt this app's collections and sample documents (as _others does for other apps), and in a change refuse set or delete of a document that exists unless the model was shown it (ResultInvalid, one retry); or make 'read both shapes' the only way a change keeps data.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":274},"end":{"line":290},"content_hash":"3f1580a73fe470bc7a6d3ba57ef57885b8c3db6293d53166746eec7261fd366c"},"summary":"A change asks the model to migrate documents it is never shown, and pins its blind writes to the current versions","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:40:08.918219Z","id":"4ac73f0be19b096d69486056c83b405cd2247a2cc06215e8409a20cec034fb05","body":{"detail":"A ClaxApiError with status 0 (daemon_unreachable, or timeout after 125 s; apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart:558-580) from publish, or from any read before it, is rethrown and answered with \"Couldn't make that change: ...\" (loop.dart:367-372). When the daemon is reachable again by the reply (a fast restart), or when the publish committed but its answer was lost, the thread gets that reply: an agent comment after the person's, so ThreadView.stranded is false and FeedbackWorker's recovery never reruns it or replies 'Made this change in version N.' The change is lost, or the page lands a version under a reply saying it could not. worker_test.dart's worker_survives_daemon_restart_mid_change only covers the case where the reply fails too. Treating status 0 as an interruption (no reply; an outcome with answered false, so the worker recovers it after it registers again) keeps the plan's rule that exactly one version lands and one reply is written.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":339},"end":{"line":376},"content_hash":"45f45da8c6e813ba2deab5474dfd08e4336e9c4d00d103ac7ade8769a951b618"},"summary":"A publish that never got an answer is replied to as a failed change","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:40:08.918316Z","id":"3834714547971ca8d68be1d2f68b6d1329b27a22544a3db287e395946bdf31d6","body":{"detail":"_recover awaits allThreads, then skips threads that are _known (queued or running). A change that was between its backend run and its publish when the daemon took the snapshot, and that published, replied and left _running before the snapshot's answer was handled, is seen as stranded with no addressed_in, and is queued again: a second backend run and a second version. The window is narrow (one loopback answer against several round trips), but recovery runs after every poll failure. Recording the thread IDs that start or finish while a recovery is out (a set filled by _drain, cleared when _recover ends) and skipping them closes it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":223},"end":{"line":232},"content_hash":"2cd25702f128ba6247722b47049051752de6131a5683c8d6b3856f08a253d496"},"summary":"Recovery judges 'already running' after its threads snapshot returns, so a change that finished meanwhile can run twice","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:40:08.918397Z","id":"39f405227bc2a9d52a680c330fdcba19bac29cc96c21cb1305366146285ce4f9","body":{"detail":"When the person comments again on a thread while its change runs, the poll queues the new comment as a second job (worker.dart:158-167). The first change's reply then lands after the newer comment, and its resolve (when the result says so) closes the thread. Until the second job lands, the Threads tab shows the thread resolved, and if the app or daemon dies before it does, the newer comment is lost: ThreadView.awaitsAgentReply is false (an agent comment follows it) and the thread is not open, so recovery skips it. Not resolving, and not counting as answered, a thread with a viewer comment newer than the batch's items (or merging such items into the running job's successor before it resolves) would keep it recoverable.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":226},"end":{"line":252},"content_hash":"70ce427b05eecce54199edc3e463a21c0cfe861210e45c0b783e85b18cdd868b"},"summary":"A change resolves and answers a thread that has a newer comment queued behind it","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:40:08.918469Z","id":"f6475fff334febf38a2bbf3de90119554c220010b80c48355b32ca979cc230c2","body":{"detail":"Before the model is called, change does setWorking, clip, system prompt, getArtifact, readFiles (which fetches the version again, apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart:89-105) and _others in sequence; newApp does _others then the system prompt. _others (loop.dart:469-510) is itself sequential: listArtifacts, then for each of up to 20 apps one collections call and up to 8 listDocs calls, up to about 180 loopback round trips. None depend on each other except readFiles on the version, so they can run under one Future.wait (and _others per app in parallel), which takes them off say-usable and longpress-landed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":259},"end":{"line":274},"content_hash":"1a4d8f3bf9c11a843b7e46b4696a76964abba67da92899cbf927e52bfa3de45e"},"summary":"Every read before the backend call runs one after another, on both timed paths","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:40:08.918538Z","id":"05037015c0898399878f1e470fd4855cfe572904ddad77d668c3ddb920145040","body":{"detail":"newApp calls _applyDb, which issues one getDoc per distinct path, in sequence, before the batch (loop.dart:447-454). The artifact was just created, so every read answers none; up to 50 round trips sit between the backend's answer and the app opening, on the say-usable path. newApp can send the batch with no if_version and skip the reads.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":164},"end":{"line":173},"content_hash":"527d170bc8e99b4e05f6d1b215f962bb00b175f62d16af002d0a494746a0bb83"},"summary":"A new app's seed writes first read each document of an artifact made a moment before","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:40:08.918623Z","id":"2a482818fd905912e0e5348c141241756e4a5a703a56a0cdfa0b3b287a6d727e","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app.md:1066-1093 (Task F8) lists worker events working, landed and failed, and ends the Working chip on the host's landed or a worker failure. A change answered without a new version (ChangeAnswered: a question, or documents only) emits WorkerReplied, and the shell sends no landed for it, so the app screen must also end the chip and drop the longpress-landed timing on WorkerReplied. ChangeCancelled arrives as WorkerFailed('Stopped before it finished'), which the screen would show as a failure. Task F9's worker_survives_daemon_restart_mid_change (plan line 1120) expects the item to be delivered again (resent); an app session's feedback is acknowledged when its poll takes it and never resent (Tier::Wait, crates/clax-core/src/feedback.rs:52-54; crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:513-524), so that test has to script recovery through allThreads, as apps/clax_app/test/agent/worker_test.dart does.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":8},"end":{"line":39},"content_hash":"661d7df218979544fa766ec73f2679c742645b9b924061a6fa52a6921aa4e5da"},"summary":"WorkerReplied is an event the app screen's plan does not handle, and the plan's restart test expects a resend the daemon never makes","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:40:08.918690Z","id":"1c659b21f1e383a857ab1b10577eafafc504716882716c9ea1c8eb3e9570a11f","body":{"detail":"Each poll's comments become one job per artifact, and jobs run in arrival order, so three comments sent a few seconds apart while a change runs become three backend runs after it. Merging the queued jobs of the dequeued job's artifact into it (keeping arrival order of the items) answers them in one run, so the later comments land sooner and on one version.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":178},"end":{"line":186},"content_hash":"737eb84223047cc5469516f63b232e62c337e670bbe243a460eb6822210505c0"},"summary":"Queued jobs for one artifact could run as one change","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:40:08.918769Z","id":"428c93fd4b4641bc47b8421b1118425da013e59fee495fb8be12af5d97730fcd","body":{"detail":"agent-new and agent-change records go to the same Timings as say-usable and longpress-landed, while TimingRecord.name's doc (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/timings.dart) names only the latter two and Settings shows recent(10). Each change adds an agent-change record beside its longpress-landed one, so the last ten shown hold about five of the defended numbers. Either the settings list filters by name, or the doc names the agent records too.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":17},"content_hash":"eb0d39cb4d6e00759f174ed06c7e2507ee8734b8bd87e9149f95e74a8b7f9ac3"},"summary":"The agent's timing records share Timings with the two defended numbers","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:40:08.918889Z","id":"94c9fb50bc7f9f0baf9df61e2e27e440b7bbe613d79758a067b5784c3759da46","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"00cc95d2374aad965d4bfde6e7d7917f5f39e930e9d323932cbd629549962f1b","span":{"start":{"line":447},"end":{"line":465},"content_hash":"ef6c465ab8a5754efeac0dc63786185156d1ea31c3019a820ba1216febadd599"},"summary":"Confirmed against the daemon: Store::doc_batch refuses a batch that addresses a document twice (crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs:960-972) before any write, so the whole batch fails, not only the second write. Tracked as a blocker on the same lines.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:40:08.919002Z","id":"72525fd1980f86e3207863cb48a8bb01ab57678ba1e600f56f3e06d262eeb0ea","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"05e6a51b1c33c5b9cf8234762fba49d2fa264448f28b25dc0fd63bfb499d8af7","span":{"start":{"line":345},"end":{"line":355},"content_hash":"50db6bb8249d747f804d8984e3aa74bbd5df9b2ee417e19dd4af646d5a5bef60"},"summary":"Recommendation: keep the publish first (it carries the if_version check, so a conflict is found before any document is written, and it is what longpress-landed waits for), then on a refused batch re-read the versions and retry once if the refusal is a document conflict, and otherwise restore the previous version with restoreVersion(aid, v, ifVersion: landed) and answer ChangeFailed with the threads left open. Writing documents first would need its own undo after a publish conflict, and the conflict rerun would then run against migrated documents. With the prompt asking new code to read both shapes, the moment between the publish and the batch is harmless.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.163830Z","id":"598f8e40966058b6698c8903736052e8b13dc8cc9f15c9055f939284d407486f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7b62817e","summary":"validateResult (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/edit_result.dart) refuses a result that writes one document twice, so the loop's one retry asks again before anything is created or published. Test 'two db writes to one document retry before anything is published' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart. `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +144, all passed.","supersedes":"d99e02cbb9a4354a4f5ccaf1ffadbdf2e5a23bec5cf2ea457c0bab6d52e286a4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.164713Z","id":"9fda1634d52ce26af3096145dd9b0ab31e517faa2304f3c2204b6e1b06bb993e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7b62817e","summary":"A result can no longer write one document twice (validateResult), and each write is pinned to the version the prompt showed. Tests 'two db writes to one document retry before anything is published' and 'db ops are pinned to the version the prompt showed' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart. `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +144, all passed.","supersedes":"00cc95d2374aad965d4bfde6e7d7917f5f39e930e9d323932cbd629549962f1b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.165368Z","id":"4dd1ecc3f2780a424cef084c59657d3bb5840e5d906017904a6b84d906912f08","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7b62817e","summary":"PromptBuilder.change takes the app's own collections and documents with their versions (trimDocuments: 8 collections, 10 documents each, 24 KiB), framed as the person's data; writes are pinned to the version shown, and a write to an existing document that was not shown is refused and asked for again. Tests 'db ops are pinned to the version the prompt showed', 'a write to an existing document the prompt did not show is refused and asked for again', 'PromptBuilder.trimDocuments' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart. `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +144, all passed.","supersedes":"2a312a4c496c2676a21964310902c8cfcb624850e95d75db092d1b345a34e004","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.165936Z","id":"1a85035c1d304888844ccec59e0ee8a11dfeb7f85f6dc125d800c52abdd38bae","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7b62817e","summary":"Publish stays first; a document conflict re-reads the versions and writes once more; any other refusal, or a second conflict, restores the version before the change with restoreVersion(aid, v, ifVersion: landed) and answers ChangeFailed with the threads open. Tests 'a refused db batch restores the previous version and leaves the threads open', 'a document conflict re-reads and writes once more', 'a second document conflict restores the previous version'. `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +144, all passed.","supersedes":"05e6a51b1c33c5b9cf8234762fba49d2fa264448f28b25dc0fd63bfb499d8af7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.166507Z","id":"f3adad798c8ebe9626747343550eda3f7f8805b7538ad5403e03779c42853a82","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7b62817e","summary":"A status-0 ClaxApiError from any call before the replies ends the change as ChangeInterrupted with no reply and no acknowledgement; FeedbackWorker recovers it (once without a registration, again after each registration). Tests 'a publish with no answer is left for recovery without a reply', 'a read with no answer is left for recovery without a reply' (loop_test.dart), 'an interrupted change is run again once the daemon answers, without a registration', 'worker_survives_daemon_restart_mid_change' (worker_test.dart). `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +144, all passed.","supersedes":"4ac73f0be19b096d69486056c83b405cd2247a2cc06215e8409a20cec034fb05","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.167067Z","id":"dd8b8b10953504844d177cd23784ce53a4f4ebcb7f601f65ef9d30b4e95dae0d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7b62817e","summary":"Recovery now only queues thread IDs; _withRechecked reads the artifact's threads just before the run and keeps only those still stranded, so a thread answered after the snapshot is skipped (the landed-but-unreplied reply is decided there too). Test 'a recovered thread answered before its run is not run again' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/worker_test.dart (fails when the re-check is removed). `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +144, all passed.","supersedes":"3834714547971ca8d68be1d2f68b6d1329b27a22544a3db287e395946bdf31d6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.167630Z","id":"95f0566fdccd1e94a7fe762ef6fcb82fe807fc9999ee41571bafa88e8d941a98","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7b62817e","summary":"A thread whose latest viewer comment is not one of the change's comments gets neither the reply nor the resolve. The reply is skipped as well as the resolve: an agent comment after the newer one would make ThreadView.awaitsAgentReply false and the newer comment unrecoverable; the version's note carries the reply text, and the newer comment's run answers the thread. Test 'a thread with a newer viewer comment is neither answered nor resolved' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart. `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +144, all passed.","supersedes":"39f405227bc2a9d52a680c330fdcba19bac29cc96c21cb1305366146285ce4f9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.171565Z","id":"3dba219782707485d43b8f65f43f1b7bf3832a802a179555d24ce4eec84d1419","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7b62817e","summary":"change starts the listing, the version's files (after the listing names the current version; no getArtifact), the app's documents, the other apps' summaries (each app in parallel), the clip and the system prompt at once under one Future.wait; newApp reads the other apps and the system prompt at once. Test 'every read before the model call starts at once' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart. `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +144, all passed.","supersedes":"f6475fff334febf38a2bbf3de90119554c220010b80c48355b32ca979cc230c2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.172635Z","id":"69c93ecd062dd7c2abaceec90aaf7edae4c822454de5741cc0127a58ec238cbd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7b62817e","summary":"newApp sends its seed writes in one batch with no if_version and reads no document first. Test 'new app creates the artifact as the session with title, capabilities and files, then the db ops' asserts the calls registerAppSession, createArtifact, batchDocs and a null if_version. `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +144, all passed.","supersedes":"05037015c0898399878f1e470fd4855cfe572904ddad77d668c3ddb920145040","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.173224Z","id":"2b497da624ccad2c800b13e6a91557517a7c2136eac51207e20610c304c047c0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7b62817e","summary":"_next merges every queued job of the dequeued job's artifact into it, in arrival order. Test 'comments queued while a change runs join one run' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/worker_test.dart (fails when the merge is removed). `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +144, all passed.","supersedes":"1c659b21f1e383a857ab1b10577eafafc504716882716c9ea1c8eb3e9570a11f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.174177Z","id":"32e8bbc13685aed323ce86330fe6d2c2d4f56a8332dba23226af1fd7a90dbdd0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"428c93fd4b4641bc47b8421b1118425da013e59fee495fb8be12af5d97730fcd","summary":"AgentLoop's class doc (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart:104-108) now states that its timings get only agent-new and agent-change records and must be a store kept apart from the defended numbers; the wiring is Task F9's, recorded with the worker's event contract on apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart. Left open until F9 passes a separate store.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.174375Z","id":"7ecd88c7bc9b7ff0adb6319b96493c1e046e5041eb40472a58905242386e4964","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"2a482818fd905912e0e5348c141241756e4a5a703a56a0cdfa0b3b287a6d727e","summary":"Contract for Tasks F8 and F9, as of 7b62817e: every WorkerWorking(aid, threads) is followed by exactly one of WorkerLanded(aid, version), WorkerReplied(aid), WorkerFailed(aid, reason), WorkerCancelled(aid) or WorkerInterrupted(aid). WorkerReplied ends the Working chip and drops the longpress-landed timing (no version comes). WorkerCancelled (from FeedbackWorker.stop) is not a failure: end the chip, show no error. WorkerInterrupted (the daemon stopped answering) ends the chip; the worker runs the change again once the daemon answers, so the UI should show no error either. WorkerFailed shows its reason. AgentLoop's timings parameter takes a store kept apart from the say-usable and longpress-landed records (record 428c93fd). F9's worker_survives_daemon_restart_mid_change must script the recovery through allThreads and the thread's feedback_state (no resend happens), as apps/clax_app/test/agent/worker_test.dart does.","tags":["contract","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.174595Z","id":"d5d5b18033d9a7963e3f6897fd33e78cc76ba80d8cc265f7d8962ca5ed09e588","body":{"detail":"existingPaths for validateResult is the keys of readFiles (text files only: .html .htm .css .js .mjs .json .svg .md .txt .csv .xml, apps/clax_app/lib/clax/api.dart). A result that removes or edits an image or another non-text file of the version is refused as 'not a file of the app' and retried. The listing the change reads names no paths, and readFiles drops the version record it fetches; ClaxApi.readFiles also returning the version's full path list would close it without another round trip.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":366},"end":{"line":372},"content_hash":"29e0eef91aa62b25772069221aafcce8b83a62717489014f9ec8b7029ccdcffc"},"summary":"A change knows only the version's text files, so it cannot edit or remove another file","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.174732Z","id":"2fa71a9b67587b005bde9a978d298499ae19896d62f9aaaa8ce182bbabda87c8","body":{"detail":"_writeDocs returns the error message for any ClaxApiError but a first conflict, status 0 (daemon_unreachable, timeout) included, and change then restores the version before the change. When the batch did commit and only its answer was lost, the code is restored under migrated documents. When the restore also gets no answer, the change ends as ChangeInterrupted and recovery replies 'Made this change in version N.' for the version that landed, with its documents unknown.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":411},"end":{"line":423},"content_hash":"0ddf73deaaf024b4b1a1c05994a39016d054bba668c71a91baf0e247c72c04cf"},"summary":"A document batch that got no answer is treated as refused, and its version is restored","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:05.174831Z","id":"488bad969f780d1544641f9e6da922d525b1f1e4480cfe190145de0cc4641c06","body":{"detail":"_ownDocuments reads ClaxApi.collections (GET docs:collections, which the daemon gains in Task R4; record 4720080d on apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart) and shows nothing when it fails. _refuseUnshown then refuses any db operation on a document that exists, so a change that migrates data retries once and fails until R4 lands. Other apps' summaries are missing for the same reason.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":638},"end":{"line":663},"content_hash":"27f41ad2f724af7892f8c80ed4abc134178c02aaca58eb0637d43b2194a866b0"},"summary":"Until the daemon serves docs:collections, a change shows no documents and refuses every write to an existing one","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:44:20.745931Z","id":"07ffd1b2a9c8a0fc69bc79ac19e92f401fa54f968cc6a10be84cae0dd64c0ab5","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"428c93fd4b4641bc47b8421b1118425da013e59fee495fb8be12af5d97730fcd","summary":"AgentLoop's class doc (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart:110-113) now states that its timings get only agent-new and agent-change records and must be a store kept apart from the defended numbers; the wiring is Task F9's, recorded with the worker's event contract on apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart. Left open until F9 passes a separate store.","supersedes":"32e8bbc13685aed323ce86330fe6d2c2d4f56a8332dba23226af1fd7a90dbdd0","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:53:53.671882Z","id":"9cdae5cb44b605f333b37f2ef09550f7c6f70469af36fc9c6142a7f4ef1cedc2","body":{"detail":"Failure: thread T has comment c1; its change is running when the person adds c2 on T (the poll queues c2 as its own job). The change publishes version N with addresses [T], created after c2, and finish (loop.dart:269-291) leaves T unanswered because c2 is newer. If c2's run is then interrupted (any status-0 call, which FeedbackWorker recovers at once, worker.dart:262-275) or the app or daemon exits before it replies, recovery finds T stranded, and _withRechecked (worker.dart:293-307) sees addressed_in [N] with N created at or after c2, the last viewer comment, so it replies 'Made this change in version N.' c2 is never run and the reply claims it was. Skipping the reply and resolve on a thread with a newer comment (loop.dart:222-225) is right, since a reply would make c2 unrecoverable, but it only holds if the version does not also claim T. One way: read the threads right before the publish and leave threads with a newer viewer comment out of addresses, so _landedAfter cannot match them. A rerun of T through recovery then hands over c1 and c2 (worker.dart:367-389, every viewer comment after the last agent comment) on a version that already made c1, so the change prompt should also say which earlier comments a version already answered, or recovery should hand over only c2.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":385},"end":{"line":400},"content_hash":"4d92c6376fb34c2c876d70c32d33a2bbdd8a7e9eae45ff7d41a03ab6bb68b20b"},"summary":"A version that answered an earlier comment is taken by recovery as the answer to a newer one","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:53:53.672030Z","id":"893b8c2bbd7b1a6e32426460f5ffddac793a08d6dbe830c736ecc65c5c3fac3b","body":{"detail":"shown is built from every document _ownDocuments read (up to 8 collections of 10), but PromptBuilder.change writes only PromptBuilder.trimDocuments(documents) (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/prompt.dart:170-230), which drops documents from the last collection back until the JSON fits 24 KiB. A document read but dropped is never in the prompt, yet _refuseUnshown lets a set of it through, and _writeDocs pins it to the version read, so it replaces what the person stored unseen: the case the shown rule exists to stop, for apps whose documents pass 24 KiB. Building shown from PromptBuilder.trimDocuments(snap.docs) closes it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":361},"end":{"line":364},"content_hash":"0308bb215668960001d5a602c1d1e9cd2c2426587b84a099503efaf053781cfe"},"summary":"Documents the prompt trimmed away still count as shown, so a blind write to them passes","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:53:53.672088Z","id":"1e7c0c0f08668825935abfa6af4b3005e8ab3582dd95a1785a6be4e9012f20e1","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"2fa71a9b67587b005bde9a978d298499ae19896d62f9aaaa8ce182bbabda87c8","summary":"A related case: when the publish itself commits but its answer is lost (status 0, loop.dart:436-440), the change ends as ChangeInterrupted before the document batch is sent. Recovery then replies 'Made this change in version N.' (worker.dart:299-306) for a version whose documents were never written and is not restored, so the new code runs over documents in the old shape.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:53:53.672120Z","id":"6fa4624eb23e8a96cadd49358f366d1be7ca24deafad70a3751b2608ae771b08","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"488bad969f780d1544641f9e6da922d525b1f1e4480cfe190145de0cc4641c06","summary":"Proposed close: GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/docs:collections is now served (route in crates/clax-server/src/routes/mod.rs, handler docs::collections in crates/clax-server/src/routes/docs.rs, store Store::doc_collections in crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs:700-719). It answers {collections: [{path, count}]} sorted by path, the shape HttpClaxApi.collections parses (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart:283-294) and FakeClaxApi.collections returns (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/fake_api.dart:434-444). The real route leaves out private data/users/<id>/ collections, which the fake does not model; a change cannot see those, and _refuseUnshown is still safe for them, because getDoc answers none for a document the caller may not read, and an unpinned write to an existing document is refused by the daemon (check_pin, crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs:494-510), which leads to the restore and a failure reply.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:46:59.393783Z","id":"9a2623a12dedb3a8169ff9a3d58ddd5353ba2da673ef6f606116a3a207ebea6c","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart _onWorker: WorkerReplied shows 'Answered in the thread' and clears the armed timing (no record); WorkerFailed shows the reason in an error chip; WorkerCancelled a neutral 'Stopped' chip; WorkerInterrupted keeps Working. Tests in apps/clax_app/test/ui/app_screen_test.dart: 'a reply without a version ends Working and drops the timing', 'a failed change shows its reason; a cancelled one shows as stopped'. The F9 restart test part of this record is still open.","kind":"comment","references":"2a482818fd905912e0e5348c141241756e4a5a703a56a0cdfa0b3b287a6d727e","summary":"App screen side handled in 9825918c: WorkerReplied ends the Working chip and drops the longpress-landed timing; WorkerCancelled shows as stopped, distinct from WorkerFailed","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:50:31.860375Z","id":"7f3f11037055d73186e0795499165cbbf8802be59e4e05b59b3c3423ab217450","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0e03ed9c","summary":"change re-reads the threads before the publish and leaves out of addresses a thread whose latest viewer comment is not one of the change's; a ChangeRecord (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/ledger.dart) names the comments each change answered by thread, and recovery hands over only the comments no standing version answered (AgentLoop.settle, FeedbackWorker._withRechecked). Test 'a version that answered an earlier comment is not taken as the answer to a newer one, and the earlier comment is not run again' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/worker_test.dart runs the exact scenario (c1 runs, c2 arrives, publish, c2's run interrupted, recovery): c2 runs alone, the thread's only reply is c2's, and c1's edit is in the final page once. Removing the addresses filter or the answered filter fails it. `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +154, all passed.","supersedes":"9cdae5cb44b605f333b37f2ef09550f7c6f70469af36fc9c6142a7f4ef1cedc2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:50:31.861544Z","id":"7c057744c354eb10b4e6176f6e9e424815bae8ccfb13cd4e2959d292c4a88685","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0e03ed9c","summary":"shown is built from PromptBuilder.trimDocuments(snap.docs). Test 'a document read but trimmed from the prompt counts as not shown' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart (two 15000-byte documents; the write to the trimmed one is refused and asked for again, and the document is unchanged); it fails when shown is built from snap.docs. `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +154, all passed.","supersedes":"893b8c2bbd7b1a6e32426460f5ffddac793a08d6dbe830c736ecc65c5c3fac3b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:50:31.862250Z","id":"766cf7d1d3a2b2e1228932b6d1d32ae6713837b79f2e481aceaeaa5056c1f4de","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:39f76d61","summary":"A batch with no answer now ends the change as ChangeInterrupted with its ChangeRecord unfinished, and a publish whose answer was lost keeps its record too (reply 1e7c0c0f); AgentLoop.settle sends the batch again with the same pins (a pin conflict means it ran), restores and reruns only on another refusal, and posts the record's own reply instead of 'Made this change'. Tests 'a document batch without an answer is finished by recovery, not undone', 'a publish whose answer was lost has its documents written and its reply posted by recovery', 'a lost publish whose documents are then refused is undone and run again' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/worker_test.dart. `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +154, all passed.","supersedes":"2fa71a9b67587b005bde9a978d298499ae19896d62f9aaaa8ce182bbabda87c8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:50:31.862856Z","id":"70459f531923e7e831a82154b5fbe440562cc252616a11edc96466819b3ea18d","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Closed on reply 6fa4624e: GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/docs:collections is now served by the daemon (crates/clax-server/src/routes/docs.rs, Store::doc_collections in crates/clax-core/src/store/docs.rs) in the shape HttpClaxApi.collections parses.","supersedes":"488bad969f780d1544641f9e6da922d525b1f1e4480cfe190145de0cc4641c06","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:50:31.863774Z","id":"dc1f8be466fb31b3b5b26490d7dce0f496125934a7355a7aba88eb78e977c535","body":{"detail":"AgentLoop.settle re-sends an unfinished ChangeRecord's batch with its pins; a 409 conflict or if_version_required is taken to mean the batch already ran. If the page wrote one of those documents after the change read it and the batch never ran, the migration is skipped and the record's reply is posted. Telling the two apart would need the batch to leave a marker of its own (for example one reserved document written in the same batch).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":566},"end":{"line":576},"content_hash":"1c7ec883cf7d10a52433addcd206637c55273451cf0955ffdad196e2b655635f"},"summary":"Recovery counts a pin conflict on a re-sent document batch as the batch having run","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:50:31.863888Z","id":"e79a755408419625660dbf5434a538b6b3ff4a9f0121a4f32f53bab009bd9dc5","body":{"detail":"_madeBy takes version base+1 as the record's when its addresses equal the record's and its note opens with the first 40 characters of the reply, whitespace collapsed. Another publish that took that number with the same addresses and a note opening alike would be taken for it; a daemon that rewrote notes beyond whitespace would make a landed change look unlanded, and its comments would run again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":595},"end":{"line":605},"content_hash":"0dfb1a07fb42e7a3553696c60f7cadfdce3d0404a9e26397007067096974677c"},"summary":"A ledger record is matched to its version by number, addresses and the note's opening","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:50:31.863979Z","id":"b1281e90c1d038e9c2135a5364dcb684c6460163f2cb170ed8f9077421113de2","body":{"detail":"AgentLoop defaults to MemoryChangeLedger. A change cut off by an app exit is then recovered by the timestamp rule alone (FeedbackWorker._withRechecked): its earlier comments are handed over again and an unfinished document batch is not finished. Task F9 should pass FileChangeLedger(File('<app support dir>/change-ledger.json')).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":127},"end":{"line":130},"content_hash":"327ce856023a927a39035acf198003d9f997717c9d814ea7589e2092ef7acca2"},"summary":"Without a FileChangeLedger the ledger is lost when the app restarts","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:53:16.748540Z","id":"561c2875ed4e1ee4429a53292d23a35e270369824430f2fe8bd8b091bfbaad4c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"dc1f8be466fb31b3b5b26490d7dce0f496125934a7355a7aba88eb78e977c535","summary":"A likelier trigger than a person's edit: after a daemon restart the WebView reloads the newly landed version, and a page that creates a missing document with defaults on load (a common pattern for settings/main and the like) makes a seed write in the unfinished batch fail with if_version_required, which settle counts as the batch having run. The seed or migration is then skipped and the record's reply posted. Checking content before concluding 'ran' narrows it without a marker document: a set whose document now holds the record's data, a delete whose document is gone, an update whose fields all match. Anything else is ambiguous, and it is safer to fail the change with a reply than to post the record's reply.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:53:16.748667Z","id":"1313e9d04e6c153ba39bf281b491e3a5843ff8240b6475b2cf0da23e8cb08826","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e79a755408419625660dbf5434a538b6b3ff4a9f0121a4f32f53bab009bd9dc5","summary":"Two cheap tightenings. VersionInfo carries session_id (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/models.dart), so _madeBy can also require the version to be published by the app session, which rules out a restore or another harness's publish with the same addresses. And the daemon's note cleaning (clean_line, crates/clax-core/src/working.rs:276-291) drops control characters as well as collapsing Unicode whitespace, while _collapse only collapses whitespace: a reply carrying a control character would read as not landed, and its comments would run again. Dropping control characters before comparing matches the daemon.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:55:53.714909Z","id":"b8f96c78d7f038d80ae00477fa2b2225edc1b3cf96d255aba837f17ebd1e379b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3d90717b","summary":"A moved pin no longer counts as the batch having run by itself: settle reads the documents (a set holding its data, an update holding its fields, a delete's document gone) and otherwise restores the version before the change and replies that it could not be made, leaving the thread open (reply 561c2875). Tests 'a batch that ran but lost its answer is found written by its content' and 'a batch whose pin conflicts with other content fails the change with the thread open' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/worker_test.dart; the second fails when the content check is removed. `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +158, all passed.","supersedes":"dc1f8be466fb31b3b5b26490d7dce0f496125934a7355a7aba88eb78e977c535","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:55:53.779358Z","id":"5ed81ea32fbe3b51be8aeba8e6736b72dcb30efb78a17adc1c65aeb5c9fbaf00","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3d90717b","summary":"_madeBy also requires the version to carry a session and the app harness (ruling out a restore and other harnesses' publishes), and compares notes after dropping control characters as the daemon's clean_line does (reply 1313e9d0). Tests 'settle a version the app session did not publish is not the record's' and 'settle a note the daemon cleaned of control characters still matches' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart; the first fails when the session check is removed. `flutter test test/agent` in apps/clax_app: +158, all passed.","supersedes":"e79a755408419625660dbf5434a538b6b3ff4a9f0121a4f32f53bab009bd9dc5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.808831Z","id":"cd30265a136551f67b213a5ff47c4e901904132b3835967d852ba94ccdf050b1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e51b5922","summary":"platformServices (apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart) passes FileChangeLedger(File('<support>/change-ledger.json')) as AppServices.ledger, and AppRoot gives it to every AgentLoop it builds (the worker's and each new app's). cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/app_test.dart test/agent/worker_restart_test.dart: +15, All tests passed; flutter test (whole app): +417 ~3 skipped (real-daemon tests without CLAX_TEST_BIN), All other tests passed; flutter analyze: No issues found","supersedes":"b1281e90c1d038e9c2135a5364dcb684c6460163f2cb170ed8f9077421113de2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.809155Z","id":"4717a344ad9f4af6e56eaa64d8b9d037226cb3d1277e616202a411d1b6d07469","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e51b5922","summary":"AppServices has agentTimings apart from timings; platformServices keeps them in <support>/agent-timings.jsonl and <support>/timings.jsonl, AgentLoop gets agentTimings, and Settings lists timings.recent(10). The app test asserts agent-new lands in agentTimings and only say-usable in timings. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/app_test.dart test/agent/worker_restart_test.dart: +15, All tests passed; flutter test (whole app): +417 ~3 skipped (real-daemon tests without CLAX_TEST_BIN), All other tests passed; flutter analyze: No issues found","supersedes":"428c93fd4b4641bc47b8421b1118425da013e59fee495fb8be12af5d97730fcd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.810109Z","id":"32065ae38a20e8b01df2ea1e69048eace27461655a3b4f0d7c1a32c44acc7de4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e51b5922","summary":"The remaining F9 part: apps/clax_app/test/agent/worker_restart_test.dart runs the worker as the app does (AgentRuntime following a FakeSupervisor). worker_survives_daemon_restart_mid_change scripts the restart as Restarting then Up with the session ended and the publish unreachable, and recovery through allThreads lands exactly one version and one reply after a second registration; a second test covers Failed then Restart. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/app_test.dart test/agent/worker_restart_test.dart: +15, All tests passed; flutter test (whole app): +417 ~3 skipped (real-daemon tests without CLAX_TEST_BIN), All other tests passed; flutter analyze: No issues found","supersedes":"2a482818fd905912e0e5348c141241756e4a5a703a56a0cdfa0b3b287a6d727e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:14:25.346276Z","id":"baaff5589c8a5e9fe21c6689c96844afc9f35cbae40ce1113c420c24bfa6cf65","body":{"detail":"With _known reduced to the queue check (the _running.contains(tid) term made false), cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/agent passes (+161) and integration_test/full_loop_test.dart -d macos passes: its recovery step (daemon killed while change 3 is held) still sees one backend call, version 4 and one reply, because the recheck before a queued job runs (_withRechecked) skips the answered thread. Either the guard is redundant, or a test should pin what it prevents (a stranded thread recovered while its change is still running being queued a second time, with the extra recheck and API calls that costs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":331},"end":{"line":333},"content_hash":"2f5a56a97800d7a0194faf34139dd0083dde3f516c735bce9486c2eae4098530"},"summary":"No test fails when _known stops counting running threads","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:18:57.770083Z","id":"33fcebc68788d0ca498e03953a9f4a9dffd7229cf25cd2c3a2ae556802197eca","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49174edc","summary":"Pinned in 49174edc: test/agent/worker_test.dart 'recovery while a change runs leaves its threads to that change' passes, and fails with _known's _running.contains(tid) term replaced by false (Expected: not contains 'threads' after the change's replyAsAgent: the recheck job queued for the running thread). flutter test test/agent: +162 all passed, three runs.","supersedes":"baaff5589c8a5e9fe21c6689c96844afc9f35cbae40ce1113c420c24bfa6cf65","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:47:42.278286Z","id":"ad59c22fd8b5a97745978d1a017e99b3ceb33e73012bae2637effb2b08ed0a80","body":{"detail":"A direct run of `claude` 2.1.296 with exactly ClaudeCliBackend.arguments (model claude-haiku-5-5) plus --debug-file logged '[AdvisorTool] Server-side tool enabled with claude-opus-5-5 as the advisor model'. In three live runs the advisor was not called (modelUsage lists only claude-haiku-5-5; num_turns 2, the StructuredOutput call), but nothing in the argument list keeps the model from consulting it, which would add Opus latency and cost to a change. The same run confirmed: exit 0, is_error false, structured_output an object EditResult.fromJson accepts, no installed plugin hook ran ('Safe mode: installed plugins are disabled'; only built-in hook modules loaded, project memory off), the OAuth login worked with claudeEnvironment's environment (no CLAUDE*/ANTHROPIC* variables left), and a parent CLAUDE_EFFORT=medium was dropped from the child's environment. The debug log has no line naming the effort level, so --effort low itself was not observable.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":128},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"866edaa88476b925d7117aa4cc77349f35f97a0ba677f9547b4a3dc06ad670d1"},"suggested_fix":"Find the setting or flag that turns the advisor off for -p runs (or a settings file passed with --settings) and add it to arguments, with a test on the list.","summary":"--tools \"\" leaves claude's server-side advisor tool enabled, so a run could call a larger model","tags":["live-run","claude-cli","needs-verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:16:42.032532Z","id":"fbd65c62c1814c4f44aa741cba8b51f1e6358860162e04bfa40ee3a250999832","body":{"detail":"A mid-stream error event (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart:310-327) fails the run with AgentError(retryable: true) and is never resent, like a connection lost mid-response, so partial output already reported is never followed by a restart. An overloaded_error or api_error that arrives before any text_delta or input_json_delta could be resent through the same backoff as HTTP 529 without restarting visible progress. Not done: the stream tests (apps/clax_app/test/agent/messages_api_streaming_test.dart 'an error event mid-stream fails the run without resending it') pin the simpler rule.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":304},"end":{"line":327},"content_hash":"9498522837aa79628d8144743880ac47cecbb2441d9198af29441f0ffdbf0dbd"},"summary":"Resend a Messages API stream that fails with overloaded_error before its first content delta","tags":["revisit:mid-stream overloaded_error failures show up in the messages-api log lines","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:16:42.032630Z","id":"812d027607255f1a231d42eb5269a652db357452a734a44115c571789ec3d86a","body":{"detail":"MessagesApiBackend's timeout bounds the whole attempt, streamed or not (the exchange future in _send includes reading the stream). A streamed answer that keeps producing tokens past 5 minutes is cut although it is healthy; a stream that stalls is only caught at 5 minutes. An idle timeout between events (and a larger max_tokens, which streaming allows) would fit streaming better, but max_tokens 16000 is tied to the budget stated in apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/system.md (test in apps/clax_app/test/agent/prompt_test.dart).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":43},"end":{"line":61},"content_hash":"b18ede5e813bcf3228893f2e870aa080782697fbb83c18e9cc83a3e4d0a0fdf0"},"summary":"An idle timeout for streamed answers instead of one 5-minute cap on the whole attempt","tags":["revisit:streamed runs time out while still producing output","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/claude_cli_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:16:42.032685Z","id":"aa2ae30039e7901554c4f8b6e29d6dc32c53516286d71e6910c98b18ecfba05f","body":{"detail":"_StreamedOutput reads 'stream_event' lines carrying a raw Messages API event and one 'result' line shaped like the --output-format json output (is_error, result, structured_output). With --json-schema the structured result may stream as a text block or as a StructuredOutput tool_use's input_json_delta; both are handled and tested only against apps/clax_app/test/fixtures/fake-claude.sh. The unknown-option fallback (_refusesStreaming) matches stderr text containing 'unknown option'. None of this has run against claude 2.1.296.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":439},"end":{"line":488},"content_hash":"49238907e3e84f6feb5ec00c647bd4d45cb0674a3648b70d946334f1e4af794f"},"suggested_fix":"In the live check, run one new app through ClaudeCliBackend with a progress sink and confirm PartialFile events arrive and the result parses; adjust _StreamedOutput if the line shapes differ.","summary":"claude's stream-json shapes are assumed, not checked against a real claude","tags":["needs:live-check","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/progress.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:16:42.032719Z","id":"914db0a5b883dff19246c3a4cebcb159edf53394845828380e4f16768409fed2","body":{"detail":"Both backends emit OutputTokens from MessageStream.onUsage (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/message_stream.dart), which fires on message_start (about 1 token) and on message_delta, which the Messages API sends once, just before message_stop. A UI wanting a live measure of progress should use the growth of PartialFile/PartialEdit text instead. Also, EditProgress (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/json_stream.dart) reports a file only after it grew 256 UTF-16 code units since the last report (minGrowth), so the first PartialFile comes after about 256 characters of content.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":38},"end":{"line":50},"content_hash":"ca30834a57e50f33dd5b8589ac887cad4ba8d5b1931d0f25881648a515423e18"},"summary":"OutputTokens is not a live count: the API reports usage only at message_start and in message_delta near the end","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:27:16.151243Z","id":"4faff43f03920cb1e22020d47257054f110814904bc508a26c1eb8295309ec46","body":{"detail":"When cancel fires mid-stream, _send calls request?.abort() and exchange.ignore(), but once req.close() has returned the response, abort() does not end the response stream: the abandoned _readStream keeps reading the socket (pings, deltas) until the server ends it or the 5-minute timeout. Only the finally in run() (client.close(force: true)) releases it, and only for a client run() created itself. Reproduced against a raw ServerSocket that streams half an answer then pings every 100 ms: with MessagesApiBackend(client: shared) the socket was still open 5 s after run() threw AgentError.cancelled; with no client injected it closed at once. The same holds for the TimeoutException branch. Production (lib/app.dart:124) injects no client today, so this is latent; an agentic loop or caller sharing one HttpClient across turns would leak a reading connection (and server-side generation) per cancel. The test 'cancelling mid-stream aborts it and stops progress' (apps/clax_app/test/agent/messages_api_streaming_test.dart) only checks events and request count, not that the connection closed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":244},"end":{"line":263},"content_hash":"b279b121ea8931a3affd2fc38be3b1f2906a5f2ce1775077a1c7e856a516a999"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the response's StreamSubscription (or the HttpClientResponse) reachable from _send and cancel it on cancel/timeout (or call res.detachSocket()/destroy), and add a test asserting the fake server sees the socket close after cancel with an injected client.","summary":"Cancelling (or timing out) a streamed answer does not close the connection when the HttpClient is injected","tags":["streaming","cancellation","review:P1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/message_stream.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:27:16.151327Z","id":"3abb59de35fe056c5fef72daf94117298d6638ddc7c5f437df8089811895485d","body":{"detail":"_block parses partial_json into input only for type tool_use. A tool_use whose accumulated input_json_delta is not valid JSON (max_tokens mid-call, or eager_input_streaming, where the API no longer validates input) comes back as {...block, input: null} with partial_json still present. server_tool_use and mcp_tool_use blocks also stream their input as input_json_delta, but keep their start-event input {} plus a stray partial_json key. Today the edit result is a text block (output_config.format) and _parse reads only text, so P1 is unaffected; the round-2 agentic tool loop will echo message['content'] back as the assistant turn, and the API rejects unknown fields such as partial_json, and a null input must become an error tool_result or a re-issue, not a tool call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":94},"end":{"line":105},"content_hash":"764c5fb80cbce46eaeb1e33f3b9b253b4c555ad127fde78193aa6d2ea3feb6dd"},"suggested_fix":"Parse partial_json for every block type that streams input (tool_use, server_tool_use, mcp_tool_use), always remove partial_json from the rebuilt block, and mark a failed parse explicitly (for example an input_error field the loop checks, or keep the raw text under a separate API-invisible structure) so the loop can answer with an is_error tool_result; add a test with a truncated tool_use and a server_tool_use block.","summary":"MessageStream leaves partial_json on blocks it cannot finish: a tool_use with unparsable input, and every server_tool_use/mcp_tool_use","tags":["streaming","tool-use","review:P1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/progress.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:27:16.151362Z","id":"c29fa07afa2159a9ac6f88034aa431919db6f38e4bf69d32845953a2604dfe9d","body":{"detail":"The prefix guarantee holds within one EditProgress (fuzzed: 9000 random payloads with unicode, astral characters, random \\u escaping and random code-unit chunking, 0 non-prefix emissions, 0 throws). It does not hold across attempts: AgentLoop's validation-failure resend (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart) and ClaudeCliBackend's stream-json runs with several messages (BlockProgress keys by message number, apps/clax_app/lib/agent/json_stream.dart:376-389) start a fresh PartialFile for the same path from empty text. The library doc says so, but the only signal is a text that is not an extension of the previous one; the live preview (P2) and the agentic loop's narration will need to tell a restart from a bug.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":25},"content_hash":"cccceb97adeed8cb28f15d5562331d99b90d1f1581ac1f644b914c382590f071"},"suggested_fix":"Add an AgentProgress event such as AttemptStarted (emitted by the loop before each backend run and by BlockProgress on a new message), or state in PartialFile's doc that a non-extending text means a new write.","summary":"No progress event marks the start of a new attempt, so a consumer sees PartialFile text shrink without warning","tags":["streaming","review:P1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/messages_api_backend.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:44:39.933935Z","id":"a28044958ad19f99970d9df6f71dca265c1965e1a686b141e243e984402e39ad","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5fbf0096","summary":"Fixed: the attempt reads the response through _Connection, whose close() cancels the body subscription (or detaches and destroys the socket when nothing reads it yet) on cancel and on timeout, whoever owns the HttpClient. Tests 'cancelling mid-stream closes the connection of a shared client' and 'a timeout mid-stream closes the connection of a shared client' (apps/clax_app/test/agent/messages_api_streaming_test.dart) use an injected HttpClient against a raw-socket server that reports the client's close; both time out with the two connection.close() calls commented out and pass with them. flutter test test/agent: +218, All tests passed. The _Connection class first landed in a9d5f160 along with another task's change; 5fbf0096 finished it and added the tests.","supersedes":"4faff43f03920cb1e22020d47257054f110814904bc508a26c1eb8295309ec46","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/message_stream.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:44:39.934509Z","id":"d5180fd20498f7a05627b3fb1e953fc261f214b1a88d936b3ba0b8b87ef7aaed","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:59fced49","summary":"Fixed: MessageStream parses the streamed input of every block that has one (tool_use, server_tool_use, mcp_tool_use), always drops partial_json, and message throws InvalidToolInput (index, type, name, text) when an input is not a JSON object; MessagesApiBackend turns that into a too-long error after max_tokens, else a retryable broken-tool-call error. Tests in apps/clax_app/test/agent/message_stream_test.dart ('the rebuilt content is valid to send back as an assistant turn', 'a tool input cut short / not an object is an InvalidToolInput, not a block') and messages_api_streaming_test.dart ('a tool call cut short (max_tokens|tool_use) ...'). flutter test test/agent: +218, All tests passed.","supersedes":"3abb59de35fe056c5fef72daf94117298d6638ddc7c5f437df8089811895485d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/progress.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:44:39.934965Z","id":"0d9045427ed4d70ee2970ee263198fdc6c389b5f550b9db86be09fb840db6dc6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:07f7a33e","summary":"Fixed: AttemptStarted(n) (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/progress.dart) is sent by AgentLoop before each backend run of newApp and change; the worker forwards it as WorkerProgress. Tests in apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_test.dart ('forwards each run's progress, the resent run included', 'a resend after an edit that misses starts attempt 2') and worker_test.dart. A later message within one claude -p stream-json run still restarts its files without the event; the BlockProgress doc says so. flutter test test/agent: +218, All tests passed.","supersedes":"c29fa07afa2159a9ac6f88034aa431919db6f38e4bf69d32845953a2604dfe9d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/message_stream.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:48:03.334903Z","id":"a2d54de05633a75ddefe737783a2d2327d81698ea1f3ddf68b4477c13c511505","body":{"detail":"MessageStream.message keeps every started block as it began, so a text block with no deltas comes back as {type: text, text: \"\"}. P1 never sends content back, so it is unaffected. The agentic loop that echoes message['content'] as the assistant turn would get a 400 (text content blocks must be non-empty) if the API ever streams such a block. Everything else checked fit: a fuzz of 6000 streams (thinking with signature, text, tool_use and server_tool_use rebuilt from randomly chunked input_json_delta) left only the fields the API accepts back, and every truncated tool input threw InvalidToolInput.","kind":"suggestion","ref":"git:727d1d0a","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":128},"content_hash":"18cae5cf9230a23cafc7b260a2aa76ce222355a77b0af3e2166126966d9f26b2"},"suggested_fix":"Drop empty text blocks when the loop builds the assistant turn (or in MessageStream.message), with a test.","summary":"A text block that started but got no text_delta is rebuilt as text \"\", which the API refuses in an assistant turn","tags":["streaming","tool-use","review:P1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/message_stream.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:10:53.954124Z","id":"92e9886546a54d002e9486db6b9544067297cee5f70aa6b0f40576fa5a27c885","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b36a9a51","summary":"Fixed: MessageStream.message leaves out a text block with no text, so the rebuilt content can be echoed as an assistant turn. Test 'a text block that got no text is left out of the content' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/message_stream_test.dart; flutter test test/agent: +279, All tests passed.","supersedes":"a2d54de05633a75ddefe737783a2d2327d81698ea1f3ddf68b4477c13c511505","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/pricing.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:13:56.157936Z","id":"275a60ebd9d3de887899ae84b6a202933cf636ccd5fa84e2c7705d1035e505ea","body":{"detail":"costOf applies cacheReadFactor 0.1 to every model and one Haiku rate card. Opus 5.5 reads cost half that, so Opus runs are over-counted (the cost cap binds early, the safe side). Haiku 5.5 has two rate cards split at a 100K-token prompt (input + cache read + cache write of one request); a long new-app run whose history passes 100K is under-counted five times. costOf works on the run's summed Usage, so it cannot pick a rate card per turn. The plan's Global Constraints state 0.1x for all; this records the drift from the current price list.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":9},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"35837ae663b934b15b44093e21c1c55815ab2ecc65d4ba3cc39287ddaa566192"},"suggested_fix":"Per-model cache-read factor (opus 0.05); price each turn as RunBudget.addTurn counts it (keep a running cost) so Haiku's long-prompt card applies per request; tests for both.","summary":"The price table is off on two current rates: claude-opus-5-5 cache reads are $0.20/MTok (0.05x input, not 0.1x), and claude-haiku-5-5 bills $0.50/$2.50 per MTok when a prompt is over 100K tokens","tags":["agent","pricing","review:A1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:13:56.158071Z","id":"c65879906d588f1a76bfe059c6a1204a8ff5e9edaa7d2da3c54a110656f58f3d","body":{"detail":"The task budget a runner sends (output_config.task_budget from RunInput.caps) and the caps the Toolbox enforces (RunBudget.caps) can differ if A7 builds them separately; a progress sink given to run but not to RunState misses tool events (Inspected from render). Nothing checks they agree.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":26},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"4adb738619b804be254684b6954ed2b34040ea3cb74519337505985f04840cf7"},"suggested_fix":"Have the runner read caps, progress and cancelled from toolbox.state (drop them from RunInput/run), or assert identity in run.","summary":"Caps, progress and cancellation each reach a runner two ways (RunInput.caps vs toolbox.state.budget.caps, run(progress:) vs RunState.progress, run(cancelled:) vs RunContext.cancelled), so A7 can wire them inconsistently","tags":["agent","runner","review:A1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/pricing.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:19:10.117752Z","id":"606dd21b5ec54fbba912015dfce8bd1eac20ebfcf777809b77f106a49348dbb0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:01a47813","summary":"Fixed: modelPrices carries per-model cache factors (claude-opus-5-5 cache reads 0.05x input) and Haiku 5.5's long-prompt card ($0.50/$2.50 per MTok for a prompt over 100K tokens, input + cache reads + cache writes); RunBudget.addTurn prices each turn as its own request. Tests 'Opus 5.5 cache reads cost 0.05x input' and 'Haiku 5.5 bills a prompt over 100K tokens...' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/pricing_test.dart, and 'each turn is priced on its own...' in apps/clax_app/test/agent/tools/budget_test.dart. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/agent: +289, All tests passed.","supersedes":"275a60ebd9d3de887899ae84b6a202933cf636ccd5fa84e2c7705d1035e505ea","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T21:19:10.118256Z","id":"0643bfe068813a57dbc4c4963d27b73b2f5de763682e871f4a078bcbcb771528","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:01a47813","summary":"Fixed: RunInput is {system, first} and AgentRunner.run(input, toolbox) takes nothing else; the model and caps come from toolbox.state.budget, progress from toolbox.state.progress, the cancel signal from toolbox.state.ctx.cancelled (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/runner.dart). flutter analyze lib/agent test/agent: No issues found. cd apps/clax_app && flutter test test/agent: +289, All tests passed.","supersedes":"c65879906d588f1a76bfe059c6a1204a8ff5e9edaa7d2da3c54a110656f58f3d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
